===== ALIF MLEK E8 U85 BUILD AND VELA INSTRUCTIONS =====
245-    cd build_alif_kws
246-    ```
247-
248-**Using ARM Clang Toolchain**
249-
250-2. Configure the build using CMake.
251-    ```
252-    cmake -DTARGET_PLATFORM=alif \
253:    -DTARGET_SUBSYSTEM=RTSS-HE \
254-    -DTARGET_BOARD=AppKit-e7 \
255-    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=scripts/cmake/toolchains/bare-metal-armclang.cmake \
256-    -DGLCD_UI=OFF \
257-    -DLINKER_SCRIPT_NAME=RTSS-HE-TCM \
258-    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
259-    -DMLEK_LOG_LEVEL=MLEK_LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG \
260-    -DUSE_CASE_BUILD=alif_kws ..
261-    ```
262-
263-3. Build the Project using Make
264-    ```
265-    make mlek_alif_kws -j4
266-    ```
267-4. The output should be in `bin/mlek_alif_kws.axf`
268-
269-*NOTE: The debug console for this use-case will be UART2, and the jumper on the AI/ML AppKit needs to be set accordingly as noted in the Gen 2 AI/ML AppKit Quick Start Guide.*
--
284-    cd build_alif_img_class
285-    ```
286-
287-2. Configure the build using CMake
288-
289-    **Using ARM Clang Toolchain with TFLM framework**
290-    ```
291-    cmake -DTARGET_PLATFORM=alif \
292:    -DTARGET_SUBSYSTEM=RTSS-HP \
293-    -DTARGET_BOARD=AppKit-e7 \
294-    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=scripts/cmake/toolchains/bare-metal-armclang.cmake \
295-    -DCONSOLE_UART=4 \
296-    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
297-    -DMLEK_LOG_LEVEL=MLEK_LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG \
298-    -DUSE_CASE_BUILD=alif_img_class ..
299-    ```
300-
301-    **Using ARM GNU Toolchain with ExecuTorch framework**
302-    (DevKit-E8 with Ethos-U85)
303-    ```
304-    cmake -DTARGET_PLATFORM=alif \
305:    -DTARGET_SUBSYSTEM=RTSS-HP \
306-    -DTARGET_BOARD=DevKit-e8 \
307-    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=scripts/cmake/toolchains/bare-metal-gcc.cmake \
308-    -DCONSOLE_UART=4 \
309-    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
310-    -DMLEK_LOG_LEVEL=MLEK_LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG \
311-    -DUSE_CASE_BUILD=alif_img_class \
312:    -DETHOS_U_NPU_ID=U85 -DML_FRAMEWORK=ExecuTorch ..
313-    ```
314-
315-These cmake options permit the default use of LCD and SRAM, which is okay since the HE image has them disabled. The `CONSOLE_UART=4` option avoids the HE image’s use of UART and could be omitted to run standalone HP applications.
316-
317-3. Build the Project using Make.
318-    ```
319-    make mlek_alif_img_class -j4
320-    ```
321-4. The output should be produced in `bin/mlek_alif_img_class.axf`
322-
323-**Using GNU GCC Toolchain**
324-
325-5. Replace `bare-metal-armclang.cmake` to `bare-metal-gcc.cmake` in step 2 above.
